WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.885 --> 00:00:15.368
During the 1860s, the era the March girls lived in, it was the custom for ladies to make

2
00:00:15.468 --> 00:00:20.731
formal visits regularly to their neighbors and relatives as a courtesy and display of good manners.

3
00:00:21.652 --> 00:00:27.975
Amy, wanting very much to be regarded as a well-bred lady, eagerly planned such occasions with a keen

4
00:00:28.055 --> 00:00:28.876
sense of purpose.

5
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.921
"Jo, aren't you going to get ready?"

6
00:00:32.302 --> 00:00:34.243
Amy asked her sister one Friday morning.

7
00:00:34.263 --> 00:00:35.644
"For what?"

8
00:00:36.005 --> 00:00:40.068
Jo, sprawled out on the bed, didn't even look up from the book she was reading.

9
00:00:41.249 --> 00:00:45.793
Amy stopped brushing her blonde wavy hair and stared at Jo through the mirror in front of her.

10
00:00:45.813 --> 00:00:51.337
"Don't tell me you've forgotten," she said in an exasperated voice.

11
00:00:52.618 --> 00:00:55.540
"Okay, I won't," replied Jo, turning a page.

12
00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.944
"Jo!" Amy swung around this time and faced her sister.

13
00:01:00.876 --> 00:01:02.917
"We're supposed to make our calls today.

14
00:01:03.318 --> 00:01:04.338
You promised me!

15
00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:08.161
Time is important since we have half a dozen homes to visit."

16
00:01:09.121 --> 00:01:13.984
Slowly tearing her eyes away from the book, Jo looked at Amy with a blank expression.

17
00:01:14.004 --> 00:01:20.668
"Calls? I don't remember promising anything of the sort, Miss Amy March," she said.

18
00:01:21.689 --> 00:01:26.092
Amy narrowed her eyes and said accusingly, "Yes, you did.

19
00:01:26.632 --> 00:01:30.255
You said if I finished the painting of Beth playing the piano for Mr.

20
00:01:30.295 --> 00:01:33.237
Laurence, then you would come with me in making calls."

21
00:01:34.658 --> 00:01:41.924
Jo grimaced but tossed the book aside, for now she clearly remembered the circumstances of her promise, though

22
00:01:42.024 --> 00:01:45.707
she obviously had not been paying attention to its conditions when she made it.

23
00:01:45.727 --> 00:01:51.592
"I'll come with you but I won't be happy about it," Jo said childishly.

24
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.482
"I won't sit there with a fake smile and pretend I'm having a jolly good time."

25
00:01:56.502 --> 00:02:00.685
"Oh, yes you will," Amy said sternly.

26
00:02:00.705 --> 00:02:07.989
"You are not going to embarrass me or our family by frowning, making rude gestures, or saying scandalous

27
00:02:08.069 --> 00:02:15.213
things." The sisters stuck their tongues out at each other like true ladies, then Jo reluctantly got changed

28
00:02:15.273 --> 00:02:17.274
into something more suitable for the occasion.

29
00:02:18.294 --> 00:02:20.776
The first house they called on was the Tudors' home.

30
00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:24.589
The Tudors were one of the founding families of their town.

31
00:02:25.389 --> 00:02:30.050
They had two daughters about the same age as Jo and Amy but the girls were obnoxious and

32
00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:33.391
snobbish, not to mention renowned for their lack of good looks.

33
00:02:34.311 --> 00:02:39.613
"Jo, I want you to be on your best behavior here," Amy said, stopping in front of the

34
00:02:39.653 --> 00:02:40.193
Tudor home.

35
00:02:40.213 --> 00:02:44.754
"I will be if those ugly witches are," Jo answered promptly.

36
00:02:44.774 --> 00:02:46.475
"Jo! Please!

37
00:02:46.895 --> 00:02:50.076
It will benefit our family to be on good terms with the Tudors.

38
00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.461
Be nice and don't speak.

39
00:02:52.881 --> 00:02:55.622
Don't say a word, please," begged Amy.

40
00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:58.023
"Miss Amy!

41
00:02:58.303 --> 00:02:59.604
Miss Josephine!

42
00:03:00.064 --> 00:03:01.785
How lovely to see you!"

43
00:03:02.605 --> 00:03:07.568
Mrs. Tudor welcomed the girls in an exaggerated voice when they were shown into the house by one

44
00:03:07.608 --> 00:03:08.688
of their many servants.

45
00:03:08.708 --> 00:03:12.510
"Mrs. Tudor, thank you for having us.

46
00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:17.372
It's our pleasure and privilege to visit your beautiful home," Amy gushed.

47
00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:23.582
Having been told to remain silent, Jo merely nodded and wordlessly followed Mrs.

48
00:03:23.642 --> 00:03:24.863
Tudor to their sitting room.

49
00:03:25.943 --> 00:03:31.346
Waiting for them were the Tudor sisters, sitting on matching velvet chairs as if they were royalty and

50
00:03:31.426 --> 00:03:33.487
expecting Jo and Amy to curtsy to them.

51
00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:39.870
Amy, being a good spirit, went over and asked about their health, and complimented their dresses and hair.

52
00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:45.032
Meanwhile, Jo sat in the farthest corner of the room not uttering a sound.

53
00:03:45.856 --> 00:03:50.398
"Would you like Earl Grey tea, Miss Josephine, or Darjeeling?"

54
00:03:50.738 --> 00:03:51.239
asked Mrs.

55
00:03:51.299 --> 00:03:57.261
Tudor while one servant brought in a china teapot and cups on a large silver tray and two

56
00:03:57.361 --> 00:03:59.883
others carried in the biscuits, sandwiches, and chocolate.

57
00:03:59.903 --> 00:04:03.244
"Could I have a glass of milk instead, please?

58
00:04:03.664 --> 00:04:07.166
Thank you," Jo said, avoiding Amy's glare from across the room.

59
00:04:08.027 --> 00:04:09.147
Startled, Mrs.

60
00:04:09.207 --> 00:04:13.537
Tudor took a moment before answering, "Yes, yes, of course.

61
00:04:14.097 --> 00:04:17.199
Liddie, bring Miss Josephine what she wants."

62
00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:24.063
Jo had to endure an hour of listening to how many suitors the girls had and where they

63
00:04:24.103 --> 00:04:26.264
were traveling for their summer holidays.

64
00:04:27.605 --> 00:04:35.069
Amy, nodding at the appropriate times, seemed genuinely interested in their affairs, but Jo, trying very hard to

65
00:04:35.109 --> 00:04:40.032
bite her tongue and keep from speaking out, decided to turn her attention to the birds outside.

66
00:04:41.276 --> 00:04:45.177
"Well, we don't want to keep you any longer as I'm sure you have a lot to do

67
00:04:45.217 --> 00:04:48.618
before your trip," said Amy graciously, standing up to leave.

68
00:04:49.739 --> 00:04:54.560
After another ten minutes just to say good-bye, Jo and Amy stepped outside the Tudor home.

69
00:04:55.441 --> 00:04:58.842
As soon as they had done so, they heard one of the girls say to their mother as

70
00:04:58.882 --> 00:05:03.603
the door shut, "What a horribly rude person that Josephine March is!"

71
00:05:04.463 --> 00:05:05.844
The other girl spoke next.

72
00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:09.201
"She looks at us as if we're rats and doesn't say a word!

73
00:05:09.661 --> 00:05:11.281
I've never been so insulted!"

74
00:05:12.262 --> 00:05:15.563
Grinning, Jo took Amy's arm and led her away from the house.

75
00:05:15.583 --> 00:05:20.904
"I have to agree with the girls, Jo," Amy scolded when they were far enough away.

76
00:05:20.924 --> 00:05:23.045
"What was the matter with you?

77
00:05:23.345 --> 00:05:25.005
You barely spoke two words."

78
00:05:25.025 --> 00:05:29.427
"You told me not to say anything," Jo reminded her.

79
00:05:29.447 --> 00:05:36.525
"I meant not to say anything rude," sighed Amy, "not to say nothing at all."

80
00:05:36.545 --> 00:05:39.445
"Permission to speak at the next home then?"

81
00:05:39.825 --> 00:05:41.126
Jo asked teasingly.

82
00:05:41.146 --> 00:05:43.266
"Yes, please speak.

83
00:05:43.627 --> 00:05:46.187
Be more cheerful and friendly," said Amy.

84
00:05:47.648 --> 00:05:52.629
The next home on their list belonged to the Chesters, another wealthy, well-respected family.

85
00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:59.471
The Chesters had three boys and one daughter, Mary, who was Amy's classmate both in school and in

86
00:05:59.531 --> 00:06:00.031
art class.

87
00:06:00.051 --> 00:06:01.812
"Good morning, Mrs.

88
00:06:01.912 --> 00:06:07.405
Chester," Amy said warmly to a middle-aged woman who was wearing a large string of pearls with a

89
00:06:07.485 --> 00:06:08.346
diamond pendant.

90
00:06:09.786 --> 00:06:12.947
"What a simply adorable necklace you're wearing, Mrs.

91
00:06:13.027 --> 00:06:19.569
Chester," Jo said, pulling the pearls toward her to have a closer look and in doing so, nearly

92
00:06:19.689 --> 00:06:22.690
choking the poor woman.

93
00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:25.430
"Oh! Are these your adorable little boys?"

94
00:06:26.191 --> 00:06:30.952
Jo blew kisses at three big teenage boys, standing behind their mother.

95
00:06:31.972 --> 00:06:33.934
Amy's face flushed as she noticed Mrs.

96
00:06:34.014 --> 00:06:38.456
Chester staring at Jo with an odd expression and the boys making funny faces.

97
00:06:38.476 --> 00:06:43.399
"Mary! You are simply the most adorable little creature!"

98
00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:46.381
Jo shouted at the young woman waiting for them in the parlor.

99
00:06:46.401 --> 00:06:52.145
"We were so distressed when you couldn't attend Amy's little party a few weeks ago.

100
00:06:52.885 --> 00:06:54.627
We missed you terribly!"

101
00:06:54.967 --> 00:06:56.588
Jo continued in a phony voice.

102
00:06:58.928 --> 00:07:03.249
Soon tea was served and before long, Jo was deep in conversation with Mary's brothers.

103
00:07:04.009 --> 00:07:08.111
Meanwhile Mary was trying to explain why she hadn't attended Amy's party.

104
00:07:09.011 --> 00:07:14.772
Amy replied with understanding, "Not another word, Mary, for it was a dreadful day to travel and I

105
00:07:15.512 --> 00:07:20.634
Suddenly, Amy was interrupted by a loud squeal, then a burst of laughter exploding from the other side

106
00:07:20.654 --> 00:07:21.114
of the room.

107
00:07:22.714 --> 00:07:26.415
Jo and the Chester boys were rocking back and forth clutching their stomachs.

108
00:07:27.456 --> 00:07:33.472
Amy shook her head, having only herself to blame for telling Jo how she should act at other

109
00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:34.373
people's homes.

110
00:07:35.375 --> 00:07:41.845
Clearly, Jo was having fun playing different roles, making a spectacle of herself, and not caring how others

111
00:07:41.905 --> 00:07:43.268
viewed her or her family.
